", "username": "EndWokeness"}, "content": "Georgia's new insurance commissioner says credit scores will be banned from insurance evaluations, along with ZIP codes.\n\nGood luck, Georgia. You finna need it.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 9986}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2119090613903835580", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATodaoEk7", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 6, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8930313, "raw_content": "", "author": "kek_saved_the_world", "created": 1794146193676, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "impera", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/buc97552/status/2119090613903835580", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Chaos erupted outside Birminghamistan Council Offices yesterday as city councillors clashed over plans to lower the age of consent to 10, with some demanding 6.", "last_comment_created": 1794146821018, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 4, "score_up": 6, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToZ4NNRg", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 66, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "dei", "id": 8929628, "raw_content": "To become a U.S. citizen through naturalization, you must meet specific residency and eligibility requirements, file an application, and complete an interview and oath ceremony.\n\n1. Check Your Eligibility\n\nTo qualify for naturalization through USCIS, you generally must meet these core requirements:\n\u2022 Age: Be at least 18 years old at the time of filing.\n\u2022 Green Card Holder: Be a Lawful Permanent Resident (LPR) for at least 5 years (or 3 years if you are married to and living with a U.S. citizen).\n\u2022 Continuous Residence: Have lived continuously in the U.S. as a green card holder for the required 3- or 5-year period.\n\u2022 Physical Presence: Have been physically present in the U.S. for at least 30 months out of the 5 years (or 18 months out of the 3 years if married to a U.S. citizen).\n\u2022 State Residency: Have lived in the state or USCIS service district where you are applying for at least 3 months.\n\u2022 Language & Civics: Be able to read, write, and speak basic English, and demonstrate a knowledge of U.S. history and government (with specific age and residency exemptions available).\n\u2022 Good Moral Character: Show attachment to the principles of the U.S. Constitution and have a clean criminal record free of disqualifying offenses.\n\u2022 Selective Service: Register for the Selective Service if you are a male aged 18 to 25.\n\n2. Prepare and Submit Form N-400\n\n\u2022 Create an account and submit the N-400 Application for Naturalization online or by mail through the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services.\n\u2022 Pay the required filing fees (discounts or fee waivers may apply depending on filing methods and income).\n\n3. Attend the Biometrics Appointment\n\n\u2022 USCIS will schedule an appointment to capture your fingerprints, photograph, and signature for background and security checks.\n\n4. Complete the Interview and Testing\n\n\u2022 Attend your naturalization interview at a USCIS office.\n\u2022 A USCIS officer will review your Form N-400 and test your English skills (unless exempt) and your knowledge of U.S. history and civics by answering questions out of a standard set.\n\n5. Take the Oath of Allegiance\n\n\u2022 Once approved, you will attend a ceremony to take the Oath of Allegiance to the United States.\n\u2022 Surrender your green card in exchange for your official Certificate of Naturalization, which makes you a full U.S. citizen.\n\nhttps://www.google.com/search?q=how+to+become+a+us+citizen&rlz=1C1JZAP_enUS888US888&oq=how+to+become+a+US+citizen&gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvbWUqBwgAEAAYjwIyBwgAEAAYjwIyBggBEEUYOTIKCAIQABiABBi0BzIKCAMQABiABBi0BzIKCAQQABiABBi0BzIKCAUQABiABBi0BzIKCAYQABiABBi0BzIKCAcQABiABBi0BzIKCAgQABiABBi0BzIKCAkQABiABBi0B9IBCTEyNzU4ajBqN6gCALACAA&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8", "author": "MajorClark", "created": 1794099227571, "profile_picture": "FIsgRa9onFDM", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "FreeFire", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "How to legally become a US citizen.   Immigration laws have been hijacked by USA adversaries.   Its called human trafficking at the US tax  payers expense.  Governors who participate belong in prison for treason.    ", "last_comment_created": 1794100757849, "content": "<p>To become a U.S. citizen through naturalization, you must meet specific residency and eligibility requirements, file an application, and complete an interview and oath ceremony.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check Your Eligibility</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To qualify for naturalization through USCIS, you generally must meet these core requirements:\n\u2022 Age: Be at least 18 years old at the time of filing.\n\u2022 Green Card Holder: Be a Lawful Permanent Resident (LPR) for at least 5 years (or 3 years if you are married to and living with a U.S. citizen).\n\u2022 Continuous Residence: Have lived continuously in the U.S. as a green card holder for the required 3- or 5-year period.\n\u2022 Physical Presence: Have been physically present in the U.S. for at least 30 months out of the 5 years (or 18 months out of the 3 years if married to a U.S. citizen).\n\u2022 State Residency: Have lived in the state or USCIS service district where you are applying for at least 3 months.\n\u2022 Language &amp; Civics: Be able to read, write, and speak basic English, and demonstrate a knowledge of U.S. history and government (with specific age and residency exemptions available).\n\u2022 Good Moral Character: Show attachment to the principles of the U.S. Constitution and have a clean criminal record free of disqualifying offenses.\n\u2022 Selective Service: Register for the Selective Service if you are a male aged 18 to 25.</p>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Prepare and Submit Form N-400</li>\n</ol>\n<p>\u2022 Create an account and submit the N-400 Application for Naturalization online or by mail through the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services.\n\u2022 Pay the required filing fees (discounts or fee waivers may apply depending on filing methods and income).</p>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>Attend the Biometrics Appointment</li>\n</ol>\n<p>\u2022 USCIS will schedule an appointment to capture your fingerprints, photograph, and signature for background and security checks.</p>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li>Complete the Interview and Testing</li>\n</ol>\n<p>\u2022 Attend your naturalization interview at a USCIS office.\n\u2022 A USCIS officer will review your Form N-400 and test your English skills (unless exempt) and your knowledge of U.S. history and civics by answering questions out of a standard set.</p>\n<ol start=\"5\">\n<li>Take the Oath of Allegiance</li>\n</ol>\n<p>\u2022 Once approved, you will attend a ceremony to take the Oath of Allegiance to the United States.\n\u2022 Surrender your green card in exchange for your official Certificate of Naturalization, which makes you a full U.S. citizen.</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=how+to+become+a+us+citizen&a